    "created_at": "2025-01-07T17:35:35Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-01-07T17:35:35Z",
    "body": "Thinking of use cases, the font relative metrics seem like they could and should always resolve against whatever font is being used for text operations. I feel authors would expect that and it seems implementable.\r\n\r\nThere's been no discussion of percentage units, which I presume would resolve against the canvas size (even offscreen canvas has a size). If that's the case then there's not much point in resolving viewport and container units against the canvas size because they can all be achieved with percentages.\r\n\r\nI do think we should be consistent between all types of canvas to maximize the chance that code will run the same everywhere.\r\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
